.TH "nvme_init_manage_export_nvms_send_change_access_mode" 9 "nvme_init_manage_export_nvms_send_change_access_mode" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
nvme_init_manage_export_nvms_send_change_access_mode \- Initialize passthru command for Manage Exported NVM Subsystem Send - Change Access Mode (message-based transports only)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "void" nvme_init_manage_export_nvms_send_change_access_mode
.BI "(struct libnvme_passthru_cmd *cmd "  ","
.BI "bool ra "  ","
.BI "bool esubidv "  ","
.BI "__u16 esubid "  ","
.BI "struct nvme_exported_nvm_subsys_nqn_data *data "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "cmd" 12
Passthru command to use
.IP "ra" 12
Restricted Access (RA): if set, the Exported NVM Subsystem is
configured to restrict access to Host NQNs in its Allowed
Host List; if clear, unrestricted access is allowed
.IP "esubidv" 12
Exported NVM Subsystem Identifier Valid (ESUBIDV): if set,
\fIesubid\fP identifies the target Exported NVM Subsystem;
otherwise the target is identified by the SUBNQN in \fIdata\fP
.IP "esubid" 12
Exported NVM Subsystem Identifier (ESUBID), used if
\fIesubidv\fP is set
.IP "data" 12
Exported NVM Subsystem NQN data buffer, see \fIstruct
nvme_exported_nvm_subsys_nqn_data\fP. Ignored if \fIesubidv\fP is set.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Initializes the passthru command buffer for the Manage Exported NVM
Subsystem Send command with SEL value
NVME_MANAGE_EXPORT_NVMS_SEND_SEL_CHANGE_ACCESS_MODE.
